OL,3,AKing talks of 'most tragic of days
OL,4,Aimaginable' as he meets survivors of
OL,5,AAberfan disaster 60 years on
OL,6,
OL,7,FMair Morgan, the last surviving teacher
OL,8,Fat the school, still remembers having
OL,9,Fto identify the children who died
OL,11,FKing Charles, Queen Camilla and the
OL,12,FPrince of Wales have laid wreaths at a
OL,13,Fmemorial garden that stands on the site
OL,14,Fof the school, and are now joining
OL,15,Fsurvivors, bereaved parents and other
OL,16,Fmembers of the community
OL,18,FIn a speech, the King described how
OL,19,F"very special" it is to be back in
OL,20,FAberfan, saying "today in our nation
OL,21,Fand across the world, thoughts will
OL,22,Fturn to you in in Aberfan
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/41
